      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another option similar to #2 could be to send the request state via the `NodesProvisionedEvent`. Though that would require a model version bump as the Nodepool part would also be affected.\n\nI\u0027m leaning towards #1 at this point. Maybe instead of a bool we should make this a launcher-internal enum in case we have similar use-cases later (thinking about snapshots, though that would only affect the nodes)?\n\nI think with the change here we could also send the `NodesProvisionedEvent` right before we unlock the node at the end of `_processRequests()`. Instead of doing here AND in the exception handler in `_processRequests()`. This way we\u0027d always send the event before unlocking the node.\n\nI proposed that as a follow-up change here https://review.opendev.org/c/zuul/zuul/+/957304",
